      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Four cases of Morton's metatarsalgia are presented. In all cases history and clinical findings were typical. The duration of the disease until the assessment of the final diagnosis with an average of three years was very long. Conservative treatment in all cases was unsuccessful, operative excision of the neuroma resulted in complete relief of pain."},
